# proxy-allowlist.messenger: the smallest door. One API host, nothing else.
#
# This is the allowlist for an agent that only talks to you through a chat app. Replace the
# example line with your chat provider's API host. Rules for every line (tinyproxy 1.11,
# FilterType ere, FilterDefaultDeny Yes):
#   - each line is a POSIX extended regex, matched case-insensitively against the bare
#     hostname (no port, no user, no brackets);
#   - matching is unanchored, so anchor every line with ^ and $, or "api.example.com" would
#     also allow "api.example.com.attacker.net";
#   - escape every dot; keep lines under 512 bytes; no spaces and no unescaped # in a pattern.
^api\.example\.com$
